## 5\. Functional Requirements

 ### FR01 — User Access

 The system should provide user authentication if authentication is included in the project.

 Users should be able to:

 - Register
- Log in
- Log out
- Access their own projects

 ### FR02 — Project Creation

 Users should be able to create a new comic project.

 The project should contain:

 - Title
- Genre
- Story idea
- Comic style
- Desired length

 ### FR03 — Story Generation

 The system should send the user's idea and relevant settings to Gemini and generate a structured story.

 The result may include:

 - Title
- Premise
- Setting
- Main conflict
- Beginning
- Middle
- Ending

 ### FR04 — Character Generation

 The system should generate characters relevant to the story.

 Each character may contain:

 - Name
- Age
- Role
- Appearance
- Personality
- Background
- Relationships

 ### FR05 — Scene Generation

 The system should divide the story into logical scenes.

 Each scene should contain:

 - Location
- Characters
- Actions
- Mood
- Narrative purpose

 ### FR06 — Panel Generation

 The system should convert scenes into comic panels.

 A panel can contain:

 - Panel description
- Characters
- Background
- Action
- Expression
- Camera/viewpoint
- Caption
- Dialogue
- Visual prompt

 ### FR07 — Dialogue Generation

 Gemini should generate dialogue based on the characters and scene context.

 ### FR08 — Editing

 Users should be able to modify:

 - Story
- Characters
- Scenes
- Panel descriptions
- Dialogue

 ### FR09 — Regeneration

 Users should be able to regenerate a selected item without regenerating the entire comic.

 For example:

```
Panel 1 ✓
Panel 2 ✓
Panel 3 → Regenerate
Panel 4 ✓
```

 ### FR10 — Project Storage

 The system should allow users to:

 - Save projects
- Open existing projects
- Rename projects
- Delete projects

 ### FR11 — Comic Preview

 The application should display the generated content in a comic-style layout.

 ### FR12 — Export

 If included in the implementation, users should be able to export the completed comic in an appropriate format such as PDF or image files.

 ## 6\. Non-Functional Requirements

 ### Performance

 - The interface should remain responsive during AI generation.
- Loading indicators should be displayed while waiting for Gemini responses.
- Project data should load within reasonable time.

 ### Usability

 - The interface should be beginner-friendly.
- Navigation should be simple.
- Major actions should be clearly labeled.
- Users should not need AI expertise to create a comic.

 ### Reliability

 - API failures should be handled gracefully.
- Projects should not be lost because of temporary errors.
- Generated content should be saved reliably.

 ### Security

 - API credentials must not be exposed in client-side code.
- User projects should be protected from unauthorized access.
- User input should be validated.
- Authentication and database access controls should be implemented where applicable.

 ### Scalability

 The architecture should allow additional features and users to be added without major restructuring.

 ### Maintainability

 The application should use modular components so that AI services, UI components, database operations, and project management can be maintained independently.

 ## 7\. AI Requirements

 ComicCraft's AI layer should support:

```
                 Gemini
                    │
       ┌────────────┼────────────┐
       ↓            ↓            ↓
     Story      Characters     Scenes
       │            │            │
       └────────────┼────────────┘
                    ↓
                 Panels
                    ↓
                Dialogue
```

 ### AI Context Requirement

 Important story and character information should be retained and supplied as context when generating later content.

 For example:

```
Story Context
      +
Character Context
      +
Scene Context
      ↓
Gemini Prompt
      ↓
Panel / Dialogue Output
```

 This helps maintain narrative consistency.

